    <innernamespace refid="namespaceanonymous__namespace_02dbexecutor_8cpp_03">anonymous_namespace{dbexecutor.cpp}</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Implementation for dbexecutor: Builds the executor from configuration, naming it &quot;DB executor&quot; for diagnostics. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file implements the two <ref refid="classDbExecutor" kindref="compound">DbExecutor</ref> constructors. Both forward the worker, queue and name settings to the BoundedExecutor base and store the IO fast-path flag. The default constructor reads every setting from the application-wide <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref>; the other takes explicit values, which keeps unit tests independent of configuration.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: It is the small piece that turns configured numbers into the actual worker pool used for all blocking database work. The &quot;DB executor&quot; label passed to the base class shows up in logs and statistics, so operators can tune worker counts and queue sizes. Without these constructors the <ref refid="classDbExecutor" kindref="compound">DbExecutor</ref> declared in the header could not be created, and routes would have nowhere to send blocking queries.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Base-class initialisation in a constructor initializer list: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/initializer_list">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/initializer_list</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Anonymous namespaces (keep helpers private to one .cpp file): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/namespace">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/namespace</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Configuration via a service locator / <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref> pattern</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::size_t: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
